## Approach

1. `str_to_list(string)` converts the input string into a list of characters so we can iterate and build the result easily.
2. `get_char_count_array(string)` builds a fixed-size lookup table (256 entries, indexed by ASCII/Unicode code) where each index stores how many times that character appears in `second_string`. This gives O(1) lookup per character.
3. `remove_dirty_chars(string, second_string)` iterates through each character of the first string, checks the count array, and only keeps characters whose count in `second_string` is `0`.
4. `lst_to_string(List)` joins the kept characters back into a string.

